tinyrun
=======

A toy container runtime. Learning project.

It runs a command in its own UTS, PID, and mount namespaces, chroots into
./rootfs, and mounts a fresh /proc. Inside, the command gets its own
hostname and a process table that starts at PID 1 and can't see the host.

Namespaces, clone() flags, chroot and mount are Linux kernel features.
This does not run on macOS. It compiles there, but fails at runtime.
The workflow below is: build on the Mac, run in a Linux VM (Lima).

GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 go build -o tinyrun .

namespaces  -> own hostname / process table / mounts
chroot      -> own filesystem root
cgroups     -> resource limits
